2026-10-05T15:26:44Z	decide	ARC-layer: Backend domain module (scoring) is the single source of truth; the UI calls it on each change (debounced) and the backend is authoritative on save — Satisfies REQ-03-14 real-time row WL and A4 (mirror Excel exactly) with one implementation, no rule duplication between UI and backend; observable behaviour is identical under every option.
2026-10-05T15:26:44Z	decide	ARC-async: Fetchers run in parallel async calls with an overall 30 s deadline; per-field results are returned (value+source, or typed failure); a re-fetch action is idempotent, latest result wins — REQ-02-01 sets the 30 s budget and REQ-02-08 requires partial failure not to block the form; parallel per-field results is the simplest design that meets both for a single-user POC.
2026-10-05T15:26:44Z	decide	NFR-observability: One structured log line per fetch (source, status, duration, error class) keyed by assessment id; no customer data in logs; no metrics or alerting — Keeps failures visible (REQ-02-08, quality role) with minimal footprint; avoids logging bank-confidential data pending the NFR-privacy answer.
2026-10-05T15:26:44Z	decide	TST-strategy: TDD unit tests for the scoring engine (full value-to-WL table) and fetch parsers on recorded fixtures; QA integration tests run against fixture-backed fetchers; one opt-in live smoke test per source, excluded from verify; >=80% coverage on the scoring engine — Live sources change and would make gates flaky (e.g. Germany Fitch AAA is live data); fixtures keep gates deterministic while the smoke tests show real-source health.
2026-10-05T15:26:44Z	decide	DEL-ci: Merge requires: unit tests + QA tests + lint + typecheck per component, wrapped by a single root verify command set once the stack is decided; verify_full updated accordingly — The kit default 'npm test' is not a decision; the right command depends on the human's ARC-stack answer, so it is fixed right after that.
2026-10-05T15:26:44Z	decide	DEL-docs: README with setup/run/test instructions, the list of sources with known limits, and the scoring table; no other docs — Request asks for none beyond the in-app Data Guide (EPIC-06); a minimal README is needed for the C1 business review and for QA to run the app.
2026-10-05T15:26:45Z	decide	X-fetch-timeouts: Per-source timeout 10 s, 1 retry with backoff, all sources in parallel within the 30 s overall deadline, in-memory cache per assessment, descriptive User-Agent, no proxy configured by default (configurable) — Fits inside REQ-02-01 30 s budget; implementation detail not constrained by the request.
